Since 2026-10-21 access in `alloq_commons.access` depends on roles alone; roles add up:
- Admin (`is_admin` switch): only the administration pages (users, roles, departments, holidays, daily rates, DB access) via `@requires_admin` / appkit `requires_admin` / `app_page(admin_only=True)`. It grants no planning or offer access.
- `employee` role: reads /plan and /projects (`@requires_viewer` + `VIEWER_HANDLERS`, `viewer_only`).
- `project_manager` role: edits planning, projects, team, dashboard (`@requires_editor`, `editor_only`, `disabled=~CAN_EDIT`, dashboard `_can_edit`). A project manager needs the employee role on top to read /plan and /projects.
- `offer_editor`: edits offers; every signed-in user reads them. See [[offer-package-and-role]].

`has_role(user, role)` is the one server check; `editor_only`/`viewer_only` wrap appkit's `requires_role`. `IS_ADMIN`, `CAN_VIEW`, `admin_only()`, `can_edit`/`can_view` were removed. Migration e023b4c5d6f7 granted existing admins project_manager+employee and project managers employee.

Guard test `tests/test_handler_authorization.py` rejects `@requires_admin` in the planning packages; guards are detected by the `alloq_access_level` attribute.

- Read-only drawer: `rx.el.fieldset(disabled=~CAN_EDIT, style={"display": "contents"})`.
- Trap: test login fakes that should be allowed need `roles=[project_manager, employee]`; `is_admin=True` alone is now refused. A refused dashboard background load makes `test_dashboard_states.py` hang instead of fail. Run per package with `timeout` when guards change; never `pkill -f` a pattern that matches your own command.

**Why:** user decided roles are additive and the admin switch only opens the admin menu.
**How to apply:** new planning handlers get `@requires_editor`; never add `is_admin` to a feature check.
